It is Sunday, and I am relaxing at home.
I open the laptop.
I video call my little sister Sofia in Mexico.
"How was your weekend?" she asks immediately.
"Yesterday was my first shift at the café," I answer.
Sofia smiles on the screen.
"And, are you a real barista now?" she asks curiously.
"At the beginning, it was pure chaos," I laugh.
"The first coffee was a little disaster."
"I made the espresso too fast and spilled the milk."
"But the second coffee already turned out much better."
"It is really fun to learn to operate the machine properly."
"I sit in front of the computer all week at work."
"It is wonderful to learn to do something completely new."
"It is real, practical work with my hands."
"You sound very happy, Maya," Sofia says.
"I am," I answer.
"I feel like I am truly rooted in Berlin now."
